rectangle "<size:20><color:#212121><b>Attention shape strategy: dense grid today, and planned flash attention</b></color></size>" as n052 #back:EEF1F8;line:CFD2DD;text:212121 {
  rectangle " " as n053 #back:EEF1F8;line:EEF1F8 {
    rectangle "<size:15><color:#0A0F25><b>A · Dense grid, the strategy shown above</b></color></size>" as n054 #back:E3E9FD;line:0d47a1;text:0A0F25 {
      rectangle "<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Pack the ragged flat list into a rectangle, so every  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>shape is fixed at compile time.  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Needed because an offset computed from data does not  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>lower under compilation (torch-spyre&#35;3508) — exactly  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>the arithmetic that flash relies on.  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Eager tolerates it; compiled mode, our target, does not.</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#160;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>· build an additive mask &#91;S, 1, L, L&#93; marking padding  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>and cross-request slots  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>· build three index lists, then gather Q / K / V into  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#91;S, H, L, D&#93;  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>· one fused SDPA kernel per (S, L), then gather the  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>results back out</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#160;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#42;&#42;Shape axes: T for the body, (S, L) for attention.  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Two sets of buckets to warm.&#42;&#42;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#160;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Costs: the mask grows with L², plus index lists and a  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>barrier per gather.  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Works today. This is the current implementation.</color></size>" as n055 #back:transparent;line:transparent;text:0A0F25
    }
    rectangle "<size:15><color:#0A0F25><b>B · Flash-style attention, planned</b></color></size>" as n056 #back:E8F5E9;line:2e7d32;text:0A0F25 {
      rectangle "<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Never materialise the rectangle.  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Each block of queries reads its request's offset from  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>the metadata at runtime, and works directly on the flat  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>list, carrying a running softmax maximum and sum.  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>That is the online-softmax structure the Spyre decoder  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>already uses over KV pages.</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#160;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>· no &#91;S, 1, L, L&#93; mask; request boundaries are the offsets  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>· no gather&#95;pack / gather&#95;unpack; the kernel reads the  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>flat list directly  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>· no per-layer index lists, so no per-gather barriers</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#160;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#42;&#42;Shape axis: block count, bucketed like the decoder's  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>page loop. L disappears.&#42;&#42;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>&#160;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Both upstream backends already work this way, neither  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>padding into a rectangle.  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>Flash attention consumes the flat list with  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>cu&#95;seqlens&#95;q = query&#95;start&#95;loc, and the CPU backend  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#0A0F25>passes query&#91;:num&#95;actual&#95;tokens&#93; to a C++ kernel.</color></size>" as n057 #back:transparent;line:transparent;text:0A0F25
    }
  }
  rectangle " " as n058 #back:EEF1F8;line:EEF1F8 {
    rectangle "<size:15><color:#5d4037><b>If flash attention lands, the design converges on upstream</b></color></size>" as n059 #back:FFF8E1;line:F9A825;text:5d4037 {
      rectangle "<size:14><color:#5d4037>· the second shape axis collapses; bucket T and a block count,  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>much closer to upstream's single axis  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>· the batch-shape tables box disappears, and with it the  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>per-layer rebuild problem and its barriers  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>· gather&#95;pack / SDPA / gather&#95;unpack collapse into one  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>blocked-attention kernel  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>· the mask's L² growth at long prompts disappears, today's  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>largest untested risk</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>&#160;</color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>Open question: whether a Spyre kernel can do the runtime  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>offset arithmetic this depends on. If it cannot, the block  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>count stays bucketed.  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>Everything else holds either way: padding seam, unpadded  </color></size>\n<size:14><color:#5d4037>metadata, warmup, compilation mode.</color></size>" as n060 #back:transparent;line:transparent;text:5d4037
    }
    rectangle "<size:20><color:#212121><b>Legend</b></color></size>" as n061 #back:FFFFFF;line:CFD2DD;text:212121 {
      rectangle "<size:14><color:#ffffff><plain>Upstream vLLM, used as-is</plain></color></size>" as n062 #back:37474f;line:263238;text:ffffff
      rectangle "<size:14><color:#ffffff><plain>spyre-inference component</plain></color></size>" as n063 #back:1565c0;line:0d47a1;text:ffffff
      rectangle "<size:14><color:#0A0F25><plain>Internal step · dense-grid path</plain></color></size>" as n064 #back:E3E9FD;line:0d47a1;text:0A0F25
      rectangle "<size:14><color:#0A0F25><plain>Planned flash-attention path</plain></color></size>" as n065 #back:E8F5E9;line:2e7d32;text:0A0F25
      rectangle "<size:14><color:#5d4037><plain>Note or upstream dependency</plain></color></size>" as n066 #back:FFF8E1;line:F9A825;text:5d4037
    }
  }
}
